# HTTP response headers for the Cloudflare Workers static-assets deployment.
# Same mechanism as public/_redirects.
#
# ONE Content-Security-Policy only. Cloudflare's _headers is additive — a
# second block for /admin/* would send a *second* CSP header, and browsers
# enforce the intersection of all CSP headers, which would block the CMS's
# unpkg script that the second policy was trying to allow. So the CMS's needs
# (unpkg for the Sveltia bundle; github/raw.githubusercontent for its API and
# repo images) live in this single site-wide policy. That allowlists those
# hosts on every page, not just /admin — a negligible loosening next to the
# 'unsafe-inline' Astro's own inline scripts already require.
#
# NOT set here on purpose: Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS). Enable that on the
# real domain at cutover (Cloudflare dashboard → SSL/TLS → Edge Certificates →
# HSTS), not on the shared *.workers.dev host.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://unpkg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://unpkg.com; img-src 'self' data: https://raw.githubusercontent.com; font-src 'self' data: https://unpkg.com; frame-src https://maps.google.com https://www.google.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.github.com https://github.com https://raw.githubusercontent.com https://sveltia-cms-auth.clent.workers.dev; form-action 'self' https://formsubmit.co; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'
